        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para>See <ref refid="classanonymous__namespace_02_peephole_optimizer_8cpp_03_1_1_rewriter_1a3fa829354b3f8b782d40175469540cab" kindref="member">Rewriter::getNextRewritableSource()</ref> Here <ref refid="classanonymous__namespace_02_peephole_optimizer_8cpp_03_1_1_rewriter_1a1ab74e93e550820b697e99a0dc9fdbbd" kindref="member">CopyLike</ref> has the following form: dst = INSERT_SUBREG Src1, Src2.src2SubIdx, subIdx. Src1 has the same register class has dst, hence, there is nothing to rewrite. Src2.src2SubIdx, may not be register <ref refid="_register_coalescer_8cpp_1a431319a3132451944eb1d97c9514e476" kindref="member">coalescer</ref> friendly. Therefore, the first call to this method returns: (SrcReg, SrcSubReg) = (Src2, src2SubIdx). (DstReg, DstSubReg) = (dst, subIdx).</para>
</simplesect>
Subsequence calls will return false. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
